{"diagnosis": "Loopback send of 0xa5 with divider 64 yields no byte received and TRAP uart timeout with tohost FAIL 0xdead after 22023 cycles. Expected recv_buf_valid to latch recv_pattern into recv_buf_data, but receiver never completes. Root cause is line 39 reg [3:1] recv_state truncated to 3 bits so states 8-9 for full 8-bit shift and latch are unreachable.", "patch_diff": "diff --git a/picosoc/simpleuart.v b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
--- a/picosoc/simpleuart.v
+++ b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
@@ -39,5 +39,5 @@
-	reg [3:1] recv_state;
+	reg [3:0] recv_state;
 	reg [31:0] recv_divcnt;
 	reg [7:0] recv_pattern;
 	reg [7:0] recv_buf_data;
 	reg recv_buf_valid;
", "expected": "tohost PASS 0x1 with loopback 0xa5 received, no uart timeout, checksum != e82517390f8726caabcc777759a3dbb48c59fd1d160e409515f1b95dfe3d420c"}

